      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page ([[write-journal]]) describes how the guarded write path maintains atomicity for file writes:\n\nBefore any file is overwritten, the system records the file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal. If the agent run fails (due to a turn cap, unrecoverable error, or denied writes), the journal can roll back every recorded write in reverse order: restoring old content for files that existed, or deleting newly created files. This approach provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without requiring a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself serves as an in-process transaction log that persists only for the duration of one run.\n\nThe page notes that the Query agent doesn\u0027t actually use the rollback functionality since it has no write tool at all; the journal type exists in the shared runtime but is only populated by agents that write.",
      "input_tokens": 5332,
